    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d43">

                <pb facs="0128" n="962" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg962"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 600.119/545a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Diplomatic Representatives
                        in All Countries </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Circular telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 15, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Two proclamations have been issued today, effective February 16, under which
                    licenses are required for all exports from and all imports into the United
                    States. Copies follow by pouch. Repeat to all consular officers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
